  "application_type_full": "Lawful development: Proposed use",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposal as described within the application would not constitute development under Section 55 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended) and would therefore not require planning permission.\r\rThe proposed use of the application site as a children's home for up to 2 children aged 5-17 with a team of support staff, would not result in a material change of use from the existing use as a Class C3 dwellinghouse, even though the proposed use in itself would fall within Use Class C2 of the Town and Country Planning (Use Classes) Order 1987 (as amended). As such, the proposal does not constitute development. Therefore, a Certificate of Lawfulness should be issued."
  ],
